{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1543161-fae-titles-as-props","id":1543161,"title":"Fae Titles as Props","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-05T14:25:59-07:00","id":1543161,"title":"Fae Titles as Props","content":"When designing a True Fae title that manifests as a prop, could that prop be an article of clothing?<br /> <br /> Also, does the Fae title of the prop have to include what the prop is or could a Fae title manifesting as a sword bear the title of &quot;Destroyer of Worlds&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T14:38:26-07:00","id":1543163,"title":"","content":"In 1e terms, the Title is the Title, and it can manifest in whichever of the four modes Equinox Roads describes (and potentially others, but we only have mechanics for Actors, Wisps, Realms and Props).<br /> <br /> In 2e terms, Props aren't a thing anymore, being functionally replaced by the Title's Regalia (and, more directly, the Title compelled to inhabit its last Regalia after one too many times breaking an oath sworn on itself).<br /> <br /> In both editions, the descriptive mechanics include that a Title always refers to an emotion, sensual experience, or object, and every manifestation incorporates the Title's tell in some way.<br /> <br /> Given that 1e's examples of Props include a weirdly carved stone, there should be no problem with a Prop that is a wearable object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T14:59:26-07:00","id":1543164,"title":"","content":"Changeling the Lost 1st edition was so good and the 2nd edition sounds promising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}